  "notes": "Complete, intact character drawings are used for every frame. No isolated arm masks, cutout joints, shoulder rotation, or body-part compositing. Seven gradual lift poses lead into two wrist sweeps using the coherent early source drawings; recovery uses the exact reversed lift. A single clip scale is applied before publication. Original source artwork is retained in front-hi-v7/sources. Small authored drawing differences remain; this repair removes the damaged arm seams. Scale v6: one fixed whole-character transform per clip, matched to the standing-idle median opaque head silhouette area. It includes eyes/mouth, so blinking does not change the scale estimate. No frame-specific scaling, head/body cuts, or pose-height normalization. Grounded contacts remain y592; flight clearance is transformed about the shared root. Pose projection, breathing and original drawing proportions remain intact.",
